                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "if you are hardcore about not giving up, then this game will put you to the test. pour a lot of time into playing each level to max out your points in order to earn your upgrades. then there is the timing, slow camera movement, and times where it glitches while playing at the worst time. again, this game will test you. is it worth buying? ---> no. how bout on sale? ---> no. i haven't seen it on sale before, but glitches might happen here too. so if you like tower defense games and want to be treated like your playing a souls game, then yeah, give it a try. i don't brag about my gameplay, but i enjoy good tower defense games, and eventually i beat them and feel good about myself. I've been playing this game on and off for years now, and still haven't beat it. mostly i get tired of the glitches and failure of the game to register my simple clicks while just trying to play a level.\n\n*+*update*+* \n\ni finally beat the game. got fed up with the fact i haven't beat it, so i stuck with it and i must say, as i opened up more of the game to play as i progressed, it became more fun and more difficult, along with the usual glitches and crap. i'm now going to change my view on if its worth buying, and i'll say, 65% yes. spoiler alert! it has mundane end of game picture and text explanation, then upon being done telling you \"thanks for playing\", the game auto closes itself. at least, it did this for me. it made me laugh.",
